WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.267
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to

00:00:02.267 --> 00:00:03.434
"The Tonight Show"!

00:00:03.434 --> 00:00:04.767
You're here.
That's what I'm talking about.

00:00:04.767 --> 00:00:05.801
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:05.801 --> 00:00:06.734
That's a great crowd.

00:00:08.901 --> 00:00:10.100
Welcome.

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:12.033
Well, guys, everyone's excited
about this --

00:00:12.033 --> 00:00:14.133
the NFL playoffs
are this weekend.

00:00:14.133 --> 00:00:15.300
This is a big deal.

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:17.434
[ Cheering and applause ]
Everyone's watching.

00:00:17.434 --> 00:00:18.801
The Eagles are taking on

00:00:18.801 --> 00:00:21.267
[ Cheering and Whistling ]
the 49ers

00:00:21.267 --> 00:00:24.300
and the Chiefs are
up against the Bengals

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:26.467
[ Cheering and applause ]
for a spot in the Super Bowl.

00:00:26.467 --> 00:00:28.367
Right before the game,
each coach is going to be like,

00:00:28.367 --> 00:00:30.000
"Guys, remember if we win,

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:31.334
we get to see Rihanna.

00:00:31.334 --> 00:00:34.300
[ Laughter and applause ]
Alright? Come on, that's --"

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:35.968
That's right,
the Chiefs-Bengals game

00:00:35.968 --> 00:00:38.767
is a rematch
of last year's championship.

00:00:38.767 --> 00:00:41.234
Apparently, the NFL saw
how much people loved "Avatar" 2

00:00:41.234 --> 00:00:42.534
and thought,
"We should do a sequel."

00:00:42.534 --> 00:00:44.501
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:44.501 --> 00:00:46.267
Well, ahead of this weekend's
big games,

00:00:46.267 --> 00:00:49.100
I saw some of the players have
actually released statements.

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:50.200
Check this out.
First up,

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:52.033
Eagles quarterback
Jalen Hurts said...

00:00:58.567 --> 00:01:01.501
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:01.501 --> 00:01:04.334
Up next, Eagles cornerback
Darius Slay said...

00:01:04.334 --> 00:01:05.167
-Whoo!

00:01:07.868 --> 00:01:10.801
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]

00:01:12.601 --> 00:01:15.901
Then, Chiefs wide receiver
Mecole Hardman said...

00:01:20.434 --> 00:01:23.567
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:23.567 --> 00:01:26.567
Then Bengals cornerback
Eli Apple said...

00:01:32.267 --> 00:01:34.300
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:35.501
[ Rimshot ]

00:01:35.501 --> 00:01:36.868
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.868 --> 00:01:38.033
-Wow.
-And, finally,

00:01:38.033 --> 00:01:39.801
Chiefs quarterback
Patrick Mahomes said...

00:01:45.534 --> 00:01:46.667
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]

00:01:46.667 --> 00:01:48.234
Either way,
I can't wait to watch

00:01:48.234 --> 00:01:49.567
something exciting this weekend.

00:01:53.334 --> 00:01:55.701
Some political news --
this weekend in South Carolina,

00:01:55.701 --> 00:01:57.300
former President Trump
is holding

00:01:57.300 --> 00:01:58.868
his first campaign rally

00:01:58.868 --> 00:02:01.434
as a 2024 presidential
candidate.

00:02:01.434 --> 00:02:02.834
But I read that his team
is struggling

00:02:02.834 --> 00:02:04.834
to find enough people to attend.

00:02:04.834 --> 00:02:06.133
[ Laughter ]

00:02:06.133 --> 00:02:08.267
But Trump is smart.
Today, his team announced

00:02:08.267 --> 00:02:10.367
that his first 10,000 supporters
to show up

00:02:10.367 --> 00:02:12.234
will receive
a free classified document.

00:02:12.234 --> 00:02:15.200
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:16.767
I feel like Trump's going
to move his speech

00:02:16.767 --> 00:02:18.801
to the parking lot of the Chiefs
game and brag, like --

00:02:18.801 --> 00:02:19.734
[ As Trump ]
Wow, what a turnout.

00:02:19.734 --> 00:02:22.200
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:24.901
Chiefs versus Bengals --
red hat, orange faces --

00:02:24.901 --> 00:02:27.267
[ Laughter and applause ]
it's a win-win.

00:02:27.267 --> 00:02:28.767
It's a win-win for me.

00:02:28.767 --> 00:02:31.667
[ Cheering ]

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:35.267
You can tell Trump's getting
desperate for people to show up.

00:02:35.267 --> 00:02:37.567
He's even premiering a trailer
for the new movie...

00:02:38.334 --> 00:02:41.000
[ Laughter, ohhs, and applause ]

00:02:42.534 --> 00:02:43.501
[ Ohhs ]

00:02:43.501 --> 00:02:44.701
Well, last night,
President Biden

00:02:44.701 --> 00:02:46.067
gave a speech at the White House

00:02:46.067 --> 00:02:47.667
and, instead of showing you
everything he said,

00:02:47.667 --> 00:02:50.033
we thought it'd be more fun
to just play a short clip

00:02:50.033 --> 00:02:51.801
with absolutely zero context.

00:02:51.801 --> 00:02:52.968
[ Laughter ]
With that in mind, it's time for

00:02:52.968 --> 00:02:54.767
"President Biden
with no Context."

00:02:54.767 --> 00:02:55.901
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]
Enjoy.

00:02:55.901 --> 00:02:59.133
[ Upbeat march plays ]

00:02:59.133 --> 00:03:01.033
-Oh, you think I'm kidding.
I'm not.

00:03:01.033 --> 00:03:02.434
[ Laughter ]
Especially in the middle
of the night,

00:03:02.434 --> 00:03:04.367
when she climbs up
and lays on top of my head.

00:03:04.367 --> 00:03:07.467
♪♪

00:03:07.467 --> 00:03:10.234
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:11.701 --> 00:03:13.934
[ Fresh laughter ]
-Whoo!

00:03:13.934 --> 00:03:15.300
-Some business news --

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:17.734
following the holiday
travel meltdown,

00:03:17.734 --> 00:03:18.901
Southwest Airlines said

00:03:18.901 --> 00:03:21.667
that they're now testing
a new software fix.

00:03:21.667 --> 00:03:24.200
Perfect, just in time for the
late January travel rush.

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:26.100
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:27.734
Well, guys, people were talking
about this last night --

00:03:27.734 --> 00:03:29.601
an asteroid the size of a truck

00:03:29.601 --> 00:03:33.234
made the closest approach
to Earth ever recorded.

00:03:33.234 --> 00:03:34.534
That's definitely
the type of news

00:03:34.534 --> 00:03:36.601
you want to be told about
after it happens.

00:03:36.601 --> 00:03:37.901
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.901 --> 00:03:39.267
When the asteroid
got super close,

00:03:39.267 --> 00:03:41.033
Eagles fans were like,
"Not now! Not now!

00:03:41.033 --> 00:03:43.834
[ Laughter and applause ]
Just wait. We're almost --"

00:03:43.834 --> 00:03:46.000
That's right, the asteroid was
super close this morning.

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:48.067
When they saw it on the news,
the Space Force said,

00:03:48.067 --> 00:03:49.767
"Wow, we really got to start
checking our email."

00:03:49.767 --> 00:03:51.400
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:52.467
Some entertainment news --

00:03:52.467 --> 00:03:54.400
I saw that '80s singer
Rick Astley

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.400
is suing the rapper Yung Gravy

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:58.300
for imitating his voice.

00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:00.300
And some of the details
and terms within the lawsuit

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:01.601
are actually
kind of interesting.

00:04:01.601 --> 00:04:04.033
At one point, he says that he --
-Ah!

00:04:04.033 --> 00:04:05.434
I know where this is going.

00:04:05.434 --> 00:04:08.200
Does it say that he's
never gonna give you up?

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:10.667
[ Laughter ]
-No, I was going to say
the lawsuit claims

00:04:10.667 --> 00:04:13.100
Yung Gravy deliberately did
an exact imitation

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:15.367
of Rick Astley throughout his
hit song "Betty."

00:04:15.367 --> 00:04:17.868
Another detail I found
surprising was that he --

00:04:17.868 --> 00:04:19.300
-Here we go!

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:21.267
[ Laughter ]
What'd he say, that he's

00:04:21.267 --> 00:04:22.400
never gonna let you down?

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:24.834
[ Laughter ]

00:04:24.834 --> 00:04:26.868
-No, I was going to say
that Astley did the --

00:04:26.868 --> 00:04:29.000
licensed the song,
the instrumental of the song,

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:30.133
which is not his voice.

00:04:30.133 --> 00:04:32.601
Kind of weird,
murky legal territory.

00:04:32.601 --> 00:04:34.100
Anyway, that's all.

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:35.667
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, well,

00:04:35.667 --> 00:04:39.334
I'm sorry for being so,
you know, defensive, Jimmy.

00:04:39.334 --> 00:04:41.567
I just assumed that you were
going to use this

00:04:41.567 --> 00:04:44.634
as an easy opportunity to,
you know, rickroll me.

00:04:44.634 --> 00:04:46.801
[ Laughter ]

00:04:46.801 --> 00:04:49.400
-No, of course I wouldn't
rickroll you, Tariq.

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:50.267
I mean --
♪♪

00:04:50.267 --> 00:04:52.834
♪ We've known each other ♪

00:04:52.834 --> 00:04:54.868
[ Cheering, rhythmic clapping ]
♪ For so long ♪

00:04:54.868 --> 00:04:56.100
♪ You know the rules ♪

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:58.634
♪ And so do I, so do I ♪

00:04:58.634 --> 00:04:59.834
[ Laughter ]

00:04:59.834 --> 00:05:02.901
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:05:03.734 --> 00:05:05.501
♪ Never gonna give you up ♪

00:05:05.501 --> 00:05:07.601
♪ Never gonna let you down ♪

00:05:07.601 --> 00:05:11.367
♪ Never gonna turn around
and desert you ♪

00:05:11.367 --> 00:05:14.300
